%N A402188 Numbers k such that (5^k - 1)/4 is squarefree.
%C A402188 See A398834 for a guide to related sequences.
%e A402188 Let p(k) = (x^k - y^k)/(x - y) = (5^k - 1)/4. Then the first four squarefree values of p(k) are 1, 6, 41, 781.
%t A402188 {x, y} = {5, 1}; p[n_] := p[n] = (x^n - y^n)/(x - y);
%t A402188 Position[Map[SquareFreeQ, Table[p[n], {n, 1, 150}]], True] // Flatten
%Y A402188 Cf. A398834, A402187.
%K A402188 nonn,new
%O A402188 1,2
